base0 patch: make the OLD end-4 ii (pre-Lua Quickshell config) work when Hyprland
runs a Lua config (hyprland.lua, Hyprland 0.55+), and keep working under hyprland.conf.

Why: under a Lua config Hyprland evaluates `hyprctl dispatch X` (and Quickshell's
Hyprland.dispatch(X), which sends the same IPC request) as the Lua chunk
`return hl.dispatch(X)` (src/debug/HyprCtl.cpp dispatchRequest, v0.55.4), so
"workspace 3" is a Lua syntax error; `hyprctl keyword` returns
"keyword can't work with non-legacy parsers. Use eval." and getoption reports
bools as {"bool": ...} instead of {"int": ...}.

What: new singleton services/HyprCompat.qml detects the provider once
(`hyprctl -j status` -> configProvider) and every dispatch/keyword call site
passes both spellings. Upstream end-4 (commit 6c041b95 and later) switched these
same call sites to hl.dsp.* unconditionally, which would break the conf session.

Apply (from ~/code/dev/dotfiles/base0):   git apply _patches/quickshell-ii-lua-dispatch.patch
Revert:                                    git apply -R _patches/quickshell-ii-lua-dispatch.patch
Generated 2026-10-17 against base0/quickshell/.config/quickshell/ii (post quickshell-ii.patch).

